# Line endings and binary handling.
#
# This project is developed on Windows and tested on Linux: CI runs on ubuntu-latest,
# so the bytes the runner sees must match the bytes a contributor sees. Storing LF in
# the index and checking LF out everywhere keeps that true, and stops line endings from
# showing up as noise in diffs and review.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Two PowerShell helpers are meant to be run by hand from Windows, where the script
# host is happier with CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never convert, never attempt a textual diff on these. `*.gif` matters most: the README
# hero animation is a byte-exact artefact, and a stray newline rewrite would break it.
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
